    {
      "say": "Walcott plays with the name itself. Split Omeros into O, the cry of a conch shell; mer, which in French and the island's Creole means both sea and mother; and os, a bone. Cry, sea, bone: a history in one word. Two years later Walcott won the Nobel Prize. Superb. Challenge: split your own name into sounds and find what they could mean.",
